Track 2: "Who Burned the MiniDisc at Platform 3?"
- Story & Context: Night dispatcher Vanda spent three consecutive months overriding yard signals to strand the 03:15 container express in the concrete hollow beneath Central Annex, using the prolonged quiet to track high-gain hi-hat chatter against the dying whine of freight turbines. Her thumb pads were permanently calloused from hammering miniature silicone pads on a pocket sampler while she balanced an optical disc recorder on her knees, drinking cold chicory from a cracked thermos. When an internal auditor kicked open the dispatch booth door mid-session, Vanda refused to kill the monitor mix, looping a shrieking acoustic cymbal transient and singing flatly through a cracked piezo element, "I trade my sleep for thirty bars of iron grit." The police confiscated her deck, but not before she ejected the scorched MiniDisc into an open ballast hopper where line runners recovered it at dawn.
